  and shareholders may decide to copy you  they put it in a nutshell Norway in the  stock market is like the popular kid at  school who sets Trends and not only that  if necessary this fund could buy larger  stakes in certain companies in order to  be able to influence them much more  believe me with more than one trillion  dollars in your Investment Portfolio you  could do almost anything you want  another example well you see Norway is  not only one of the richest countries in  the world it is also one of the most  egalitarian and it is precisely this  social model that they try to bring to  their companies in fact do you know what  one of the major causes Norway is  fighting for exactly the salary of  managers Norway has been pressuring  companies for years to other high  salaries they pay to their managers this  means one thing the Norwegian Sovereign  wealth fund could end up becoming a  nightmare for CEOs that's why headlines  like this one don't come as a surprise  world's largest Sovereign wealth fund to  vote against Apple's CEO Tim Cook's pay  package and keep in mind the problem is  that you can start with the salary of  managers and end up with many other  initiatives let's say that if necessary  Norway could use the fund as a political  weapon in One Direction or the other  [Music]  this year the fund announced that it  will liquidate all its Russian assets  we're talking about 2.8 billion dollars  it's not a large sum if we compare it  with the other Investments they have in  other countries but there it is and  logically the more money the fund has  the more influence it has so if one  thing is clear it is that the huge  torrent of money that is now pouring  into the lands of fjords will if  anything greatly increase that influence  there are those who have harshly  criticized the Norwegian Sovereign  wealth fund for Its Behavior why because  pursuing political or ideological  interests when investing can result in  Lost returns and this could be bad 